1
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:04,300
[GUNSHOTS]

2
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:07,180
Elizabeth! Hey! What's going on?

3
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:18,560
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

4
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:23,980
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

5
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:33,860
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

6
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:36,540
nezumiiro no sora no shita

7
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:42,840
Higawari no chizu
ikutsumo no yume ga nijinde ita

8
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:48,960
Itsuka wa sa chippoke na
boku no kono hohaba demo

9
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:55,040
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

10
00:00:55,180 --> 00:01:01,200
Tsuyogatte kizutsuita kokoro sukashita you ni

11
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:08,080
Furidashita amatsubutachi ga
ranhansha kurikaesu

12
00:01:08,260 --> 00:01:13,620
Massugu na hikari ga kousa shite

13
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:20,340
Yukusaki mo tsugenu mama
dokomademo tsukinukeru

14
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:26,100
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakistukete

15
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:32,300
Kono sora no shita donna toko ni ite mo

16
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:39,120
Todoku hazu nanda mada minu sekai e

17
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:41,940
Subtitles from Mohamed610 corrected by somanypetals.

18
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:45,500
So this piece of info was
supposed to be confidential...

19
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:47,160
...but, whatever.

20
00:01:47,420 --> 00:01:51,380
Barry told me the Colonel's got a plan
to smoke out some military guys he's been after.

21
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:53,680
The ones from "The Fifth" something or other.

22
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,200
The Fifth Laboratory.

23
00:01:58,300 --> 00:01:59,240
Al?

24
00:01:59,820 --> 00:02:01,240
I gotta find him.

25
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:04,040
This could lead us straight to the
person who killed Lieutenant Hughes.

26
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:05,260
Huh?!

27
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:08,340
Hey, not so fast!
Tell me your secret first!

28
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,740
I'll tell you when I get back, okay?

29
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,600
Oh, come on! That's so unfair!

30
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,080
I'll be back soon.

31
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:21,060
Okay. Just be careful.

32
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:24,300
I will. I promise.

33
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:33,020
[GUN CLICKING EMPTY]

34
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:37,360
Are you all done now?

35
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,680
Then it's time to eat you.

36
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:45,260
[BARKING]

37
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:47,060
[GROWLING]

38
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:53,540
Stop it! That tickles!

39
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:54,840
Catch!

40
00:02:57,660 --> 00:03:00,380
[GUNSHOTS]

41
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:05,880
[GUN CLICKING EMPTY]

42
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:15,080
Bullets gone? Goodie, goodie!
I get to have dinner and dessert!

43
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,500
I barely made it.

44
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:27,980
[RELIEVED EXHALE]

45
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:29,600
Colonel!

46
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:31,580
Why the hell did you leave your post?!

47
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:32,240
Uh—!

48
00:03:32,820 --> 00:03:36,120
No matter what happened to us, you could
still have kept your involvement a secret!

49
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:37,680
That was the whole idea, right?

50
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:40,340
But you just come waltzing in here, plain as day!

51
00:03:40,340 --> 00:03:41,960
Are you a complete idiot?!

52
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:46,420
MUSTANG: Yeah, fine, fine, that's it. I'm an idiot, happy?
[FUERY CHUCKLING]

53
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:50,560
Who the heck was that fat guy?

54
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:54,460
Colonel! The target's on the move, sir!

55
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:57,520
Strike the camp, sergeant!
Don't leave a single trace!

56
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:00,640
And you stay right by the
sergeant's side, Hayate Sir!

57
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:01,800
- Sir!
- [BARKS]

58
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:03,720
[FOOTSTEPS]

59
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:05,220
Colonel.

60
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,240
What is it?

61
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:08,420
Thanks for saving us back there.

62
00:04:08,780 --> 00:04:12,000
Tell me later.
Let's just stay focused on the mission for now.

63
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,000
Sir.

64
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:19,700
Quick, get in!

65
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:20,580
Yes, sir.

66
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:27,560
Are you trying to go after
Mr. Hughes' murderer?

67
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,100
You in?

68
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:33,460
Yeah!

69
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:40,400
Don't let him get away.

70
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:41,960
He ain't going nowhere.

71
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,200
[LAUGHS]

72
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:45,160
My soul won't be able to rest.

73
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:48,260
Not until I eviscerate that meatbag!

74
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:52,640
So do you think we can expect another
appearance from that blubberbeast back there?

75
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:55,480
I doubt it. I scorched him off the ledge.

76
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:59,280
Yeah, and I shot him in the head,
but he didn't really seem to mind.

77
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:00,000
[GASPS]

78
00:05:00,340 --> 00:05:03,100
He didn't have an Ouroboros tattoo, did he?

79
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,940
A tattoo? Well...

80
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,240
Actually, yeah. On his tongue.

81
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:14,000
In that case, you were probably dealing with a Homunculus.

82
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:17,160
[BARRY SCREAMING]

83
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:18,360
Watch it, Mustang!

84
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:21,340
Hold on a damn second.
What are you saying, Al?

85
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:23,040
That's just not possible.

86
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:27,180
Yeah, that's what I thought.
Until I got kidnapped by a Homunculus.

87
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:28,980
He called himself Greed.

88
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:32,360
One thing he told me
is that nothing is impossible.

89
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:36,320
I know for a fact that they
have amazing healing powers.

90
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:42,620
I watched Greed get the top half of his head knocked off,
but he was perfectly fine a minute later.

91
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:44,080
They're real, all right.

92
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:46,700
But I understand if you don't believe me.

93
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:50,120
After what I just saw, I have to believe you.

94
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:54,000
Hold on, I rendered Fatboy down
to a bubbling puddle back there.

95
00:05:54,060 --> 00:05:55,940
Are you telling me he's still alive?

96
00:05:56,520 --> 00:05:57,480
AL: Probably.

97
00:05:57,760 --> 00:05:59,440
MUSTANG: Tch. Wonderful!

98
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:02,600
Just a never-ending
parade of freaks lately, huh?

99
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:18,940
BARRY: My body ran in there.
Seems to think it can hide from me.

100
00:06:19,020 --> 00:06:20,780
MUSTANG: The Third Laboratory, huh?

101
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:24,320
So this ties them directly to the military.

102
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:27,960
That's all we need for now.
We're pulling back.

103
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:30,540
BARRY: Well, you have fun with that!
MUSTANG: Get back here!

104
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:34,320
HAVOC: That psycho stormed the building.

105
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:36,580
Yep, it's our lucky day.

106
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:37,400
Huh?

107
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:38,820
[BARRY GIGGLING MANIACALLY]

108
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:40,120
[PEOPLE SCREAMING]

109
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:42,940
Out of my way!

110
00:06:42,980 --> 00:06:46,020
I don't want any of your boring old skin and bones.

111
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:48,880
I got me a special reunion to get to.

112
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:54,280
All personnel must evacuate immediately!

113
00:06:55,060 --> 00:06:56,160
Um, Colonel?

114
00:06:56,380 --> 00:06:59,420
Stay back. The man who broke in is a deranged murderer.

115
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:01,480
My men will handle his capture.

116
00:07:01,760 --> 00:07:03,860
Order your guards to seal off the exits!

117
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Yes, sir!

118
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:17,440
HAVOC: How the hell are we
supposed to find him?

119
00:07:19,420 --> 00:07:21,140
We're gonna have to split up.

120
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:21,880
Yes, sir.

121
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:34,640
It doesn't look like anybody's
used this lab in a while.

122
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:37,640
I guess not. What is this stuff?

123
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:39,480
I have no idea.

124
00:07:39,780 --> 00:07:42,600
But whatever they did here
was painful for someone.

125
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:45,400
Well now,
I am just shocked.

126
00:07:49,160 --> 00:07:52,040
It's bad enough that you
stood me up on our date.

127
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:55,280
And now you point a gun at me?

128
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:58,740
You've got some nerve,
don't you?

129
00:07:58,800 --> 00:07:59,920
Solaris?

130
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:02,220
What's going on?

131
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:03,580
Hey, Havoc...

132
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:06,000
Your girl's got the tattoo.

133
00:08:06,180 --> 00:08:09,000
HAVOC: Yeah. First I've seen it, sir.

134
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:13,160
Quit staring.
It's not very polite.

135
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:16,520
MUSTANG: Well, I can see how
she tricked you so easily.

136
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:18,840
You've always been
a sucker for big boobs.

137
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:24,200
[CRYING] I can't help it! I love 'em!

138
00:08:26,620 --> 00:08:28,380
Did you tell this woman anything?

139
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:31,560
No. I never said a single
thing about work, sir!

140
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:38,400
Tell me. Do you know who Maes Hughes is?

141
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:43,360
Oh, yes. He was quite the
intelligent man, wouldn't you agree?

142
00:08:43,540 --> 00:08:46,180
I only wish I'd had the opportunity to pick his brain

143
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:47,000
[GUNSHOT]

144
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,260
On your knees!

145
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:52,600
I wanna know everything.

146
00:08:53,380 --> 00:08:55,000
Sorry to say...

147
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:59,360
But it's gonna take more than you're
capable of to make me get on my—

148
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:01,360
[GUNSHOTS]

149
00:09:05,260 --> 00:09:09,740
How merciless. Did you pick that up in Ishval, huh?

150
00:09:12,700 --> 00:09:14,200
You're a Homunculus.

151
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:17,300
Indeed. How very astute of you, Jean.

152
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:19,440
But I doubt you've seen this one.

153
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:28,720
Take a good look, boys. It's a Philosopher's Stone.

154
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:32,420
I was created with this stone at my core.

155
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:36,180
It's not just a legend, it's my heart.

156
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:38,160
You're a monster.

157
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:40,080
That was uncalled for.

158
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:41,860
I do have feelings.

159
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:45,700
Apart from a few things, I was
made nearly identical to you.

160
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:48,260
I am human.

161
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:53,300
MUSTANG: I've got a funny feeling the
only reason you're telling us this...

162
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:55,380
is because you don't
plan on letting us live.

163
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:58,000
Yep. It's such a shame.

164
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:03,000
Too slow!

165
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:09,780
Oh no, did I get your
ignition glove all wet?

166
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:11,300
Silly me.

167
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:13,300
[BOTH YELLING]

168
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:21,120
What are we gonna do? She'll shred us with her freaky fingers!

169
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,980
No, she made a big mistake.

170
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:26,480
She flooded the room with water.

171
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:31,000
A simple transmutation
and we've got hydrogen gas.

172
00:10:39,060 --> 00:10:40,720
[BOTH GASP]

173
00:10:46,260 --> 00:10:47,760
Fullmetal Alchemist.

174
00:10:49,540 --> 00:10:51,700
Fullmetal Alchemist.

175
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:54,060
HAVOC: Aw...

176
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:58,380
Crap. This was a gift from
one of my ex-girlfriends.

177
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:01,340
Man.

178
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:04,740
Hey, Colonel.
You mind giving me a light here?

179
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,880
Oh, right. You're all wet.

180
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:10,020
Yeah, well those things will
kill you, you know that?!

181
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:14,240
She's dust. I definitely cremated her.

182
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:16,000
How do you know for sure, sir?

183
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:17,440
The stench.

184
00:11:17,620 --> 00:11:20,080
I'm pretty familiar with that stink by now.

185
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:22,380
You mean from that
time you spent in Ishval?

186
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:24,780
For all we know, she
could still regenerate.

187
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:26,500
So stay alert.

188
00:11:26,540 --> 00:11:27,100
Yes, sir.

189
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:30,000
Ah!

190
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:35,900
Havoc!

191
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:43,280
MUSTANG: Havoc, hang in there.

192
00:11:43,460 --> 00:11:45,200
LUST: Don't kid yourself.

193
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:47,320
[LAUGHS]
He's a dead man.

194
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:50,360
No, he's not.

195
00:11:52,700 --> 00:11:53,560
Give up.

196
00:11:53,740 --> 00:11:56,400
There's nothing you can do that'll kill me.

197
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:59,560
Then you won't mind if I borrow this!

198
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:13,280
I need it to save Havoc.

199
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:22,460
I don't know that much about medicinal alchemy,
but this should amplify my abilities.

200
00:12:24,940 --> 00:12:27,920
It seems like you should buy a girl dinner first,

201
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,760
before you stick your hand in her chest.

202
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:45,000
Uh...your Excellency!

203
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:47,900
What's the current status?

204
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:52,520
The criminal responsible for the
prison break has stormed the premises.

205
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:54,940
But Colonel Mustang
and his men are in pursuit.

206
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:58,500
Well then, I'll give him some backup.

207
00:12:58,620 --> 00:13:00,720
Very good. We're right behind you, sir.

208
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:01,740
No.

209
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:05,680
I'd prefer to handle it on my own.

210
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:09,160
[LAUGHS]

211
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:10,440
I told you.

212
00:13:10,940 --> 00:13:13,040
The Philosopher's Stone's my core.

213
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:20,420
I really hate to do this.

214
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:23,580
You were a prime
candidate for sacrifice and all.

215
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:26,000
But you forced me to kill you.

216
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:27,480
God damn you.

217
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:29,480
[GLOVE TEARING]

218
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,240
Save your breath.

219
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:33,700
I want you to watch
poor Jean bleed to death.

220
00:13:33,740 --> 00:13:35,440
Then you can die.

221
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:38,640
Jean.

222
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:39,820
Hey.

223
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:41,460
Answer me.

224
00:13:41,580 --> 00:13:42,660
Havoc!

225
00:13:42,940 --> 00:13:44,320
You can't die.

226
00:13:44,540 --> 00:13:47,280
Not yet. Not before I do.

227
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:49,820
Havoc...

228
00:13:58,380 --> 00:13:59,500
BARRY: Sorry.

229
00:13:59,620 --> 00:14:01,240
But you got here too late.

230
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,440
Look at this mess.

231
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:06,340
My body is damn near entirely decayed.

232
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:11,180
I guess a body just can't hold up with
someone else's soul being shoved inside of it.

233
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:12,460
[AL GASPS]

234
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:18,140
If a soul is incompatible
with another person's body...

235
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:22,540
wouldn't it be the same for a
soul bonded to a suit of armor?

236
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:24,360
If that's right...

237
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:30,000
There's no guarantee I'll be able to stay in
this form long enough to get our old bodies back.

238
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:31,880
Brother.

239
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:38,020
I was wondering when you
were going to show up, Lusty.

240
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:39,740
Number 66.

241
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:42,360
Care to explain why
you're helping the Colonel?

242
00:14:42,900 --> 00:14:45,060
I thought it'd be fun to switch things up.

243
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:50,120
Besides, I've wanted to
chop you up since I met you.

244
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,220
You're such a handful, 66.

245
00:14:53,380 --> 00:14:55,780
And I'm sad to see you here, Armor Boy.

246
00:14:55,820 --> 00:14:57,740
You just had to tag along.

247
00:14:57,880 --> 00:14:59,900
Talk about a setback.

248
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:05,900
It's bad enough to lose one, but now you're
forcing me to kill a second candidate.

249
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:07,520
AL: Candidate?

250
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:09,020
A second one?

251
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:10,060
Yeah.

252
00:15:10,180 --> 00:15:11,900
You and Mr. Gallantry.

253
00:15:11,980 --> 00:15:14,400
That's enough of the
casual chit-chat, Lust!

254
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:18,000
All I want to hear from you is screaming!

255
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:29,840
I do hate overconfident men.

256
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:32,180
Now then, where were we?

257
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:35,980
I think I was about to send the
Lieutenant to join her superior.

258
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:36,780
[GASPS]

259
00:15:43,820 --> 00:15:45,300
Wait a minute.

260
00:15:45,780 --> 00:15:48,940
So when you said you'd already
had to kill someone...

261
00:15:49,380 --> 00:15:50,700
It can't be.

262
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:52,240
You didn't!

263
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:53,680
[CHUCKLES]

264
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:55,380
[GASPS]

265
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:57,400
You bitch!

266
00:15:57,400 --> 00:15:59,240
[CONTINUOUS GUNFIRE]

267
00:15:59,240 --> 00:16:01,140
[HAWKEYE SCREAMING]

268
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,960
[GUN CLICKING EMPTY]

269
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:12,960
[GUNFIRE CONTINUES]

270
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:17,160
[HAWKEYE SOBBING]

271
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:19,160
[GUN CLICKS EMPTY]

272
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:23,600
Are you done?

273
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:45,000
Such a sad and weak creature.

274
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:47,000
Another typical human.

275
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:54,500
Stand up, Lieutenant. You need to get out of here.

276
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:57,000
LUST: Do you want me to kill you first?

277
00:16:59,380 --> 00:17:00,660
[GASPS]

278
00:17:01,180 --> 00:17:02,260
Oh my.

279
00:17:02,420 --> 00:17:04,820
It appears you've opened the portal.

280
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:10,660
Such a shame.

281
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:13,320
You are a perfect candidate.

282
00:17:17,100 --> 00:17:20,520
HAWKEYE: Listen, Alphonse,
leave me and save yourself.

283
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:21,300
AL: No!

284
00:17:21,340 --> 00:17:22,420
Run!

285
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:24,600
- I won't!
- Go!

286
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,780
I won't leave you!

287
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:32,860
I'm sick of watching people die, and I
can't just sit back and take it anymore!

288
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:35,200
I won't let anyone else get killed!

289
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:37,520
Not when I can protect them!

290
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:44,260
Well spoken.

291
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:46,600
I couldn't agree more.

292
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:47,440
[GASP]

293
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:51,900
[LUST SCREAMING]

294
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:01,820
MUSTANG: Looks like I can get you
on your knees, after all.

295
00:18:06,260 --> 00:18:08,340
LUST: He's using the flint for ignition...

296
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:11,520
And he carved a
transmutation circle into his hand!

297
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:16,000
You should have bled
to death by now!

298
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
I seared the wound closed.

299
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:21,300
I came close to passing out from the pain.

300
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:27,860
You told me I couldn't kill you.

301
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:30,720
But I'd like to try
and prove you wrong!

302
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:35,000
So let's see.
How many times is it gonna take?

303
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:37,860
[LUST SCREAMING]

304
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:38,920
Colonel!

305
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:45,160
[LUST SCREAMING] No!

306
00:18:46,740 --> 00:18:48,720
[LUST SCREAMING]

307
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:14,240
You killed me.

308
00:19:15,380 --> 00:19:17,060
I hate losing.

309
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:21,120
But there are worse ways to die
than at the hands of a man like you.

310
00:19:21,540 --> 00:19:24,600
I love how cold and
focused your eyes are.

311
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:27,080
I look forward...

312
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:30,960
to the day when those eyes will be wide with agony.

313
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:32,580
It's coming.

314
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:34,280
It's coming...

315
00:19:42,840 --> 00:19:43,920
Colonel!

316
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:48,000
Are you alright?

317
00:19:48,060 --> 00:19:50,360
Forget about me.
We need to get you some help.

318
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:52,220
Thanks, Alphonse.

319
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:55,000
Thank you for looking
after my subordinate.

320
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:57,660
Yeah, sure.
We need to call you a doctor.

321
00:19:57,740 --> 00:19:59,960
Oh, yeah. Hurry.

322
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:01,920
Call a doctor for Havoc.

323
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:03,980
Please.

324
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:16,240
He's alright... He's alright...

325
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:22,280
[GASP]

326
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:32,700
Uh, hey.
I'm home now.

327
00:20:36,320 --> 00:20:38,660
Moron! Welcome back!

328
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:41,900
Uh...okay! Thanks?

329
00:20:43,500 --> 00:20:47,800
Well...uh...

330
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:51,520
[WINRY LAUGHING]

331
00:20:51,620 --> 00:20:54,400
[BOTH LAUGHING]

332
00:20:54,460 --> 00:20:56,700
[CRASH]
[BOTH YELLING]

333
00:20:56,760 --> 00:20:57,940
WINRY: That shouldn't happen!

334
00:20:57,980 --> 00:20:59,440
AL: It won't stay!

335
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:01,720
AL: Ah! I can't put it back on!

336
00:21:05,360 --> 00:21:09,220
BARRY: Holy moly!
That was way too damn close.

337
00:21:09,460 --> 00:21:11,260
I hope someone can fix me.

338
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:14,980
I'd rather not live
my life as sheet metal.

339
00:21:16,060 --> 00:21:21,000
Ahh—what the...
How the hell are you still alive?!

340
00:21:21,060 --> 00:21:24,240
Hey! Oh, no!
Put me down right now!

341
00:21:24,380 --> 00:21:27,180
I-I've got a second
chance to terrorize the city!

342
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:28,840
You're gonna ruin everything!

343
00:21:28,900 --> 00:21:30,920
No! Don't do it! Wait!

344
00:21:30,980 --> 00:21:34,000
No! Stop! Please!

345
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:38,200
[BARRY'S BODY THUDS]

346
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:46,640
[INDISCERNIBLE]

347
00:21:46,780 --> 00:21:47,940
[TWINKLE]

348
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:11,160
It can't be...

349
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:15,920
Is it?

350
00:22:22,860 --> 00:22:24,320
[GASPS]

351
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:27,100
Hohenheim!

352
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:34,400
Let it all out, let it all out

353
00:22:34,400 --> 00:22:38,760
Tsuyogaranakute ii n da ne

354
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:45,100
Dareka ga kaite'tta

355
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:51,120
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

356
00:22:51,580 --> 00:22:56,820
Jibunrashisa nante, dare mo wakaranai yo

357
00:22:56,820 --> 00:23:02,200
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu
de nakushitari, hirottari, 

358
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:11,960
Kyuu ni samishiku natte,
naichau hi mo aru kedo

359
00:23:12,160 --> 00:23:17,580
Namida mo itami mo, hoshi ni kaeyou

360
00:23:17,660 --> 00:23:23,840
Ashita wo terasu akari wo tomosou

361
00:23:23,840 --> 00:23:31,780
Chiisana te kazashite
futari de tsukurou hoshikuzu wo

362
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:34,040
Tsuyoku hikaru ein wo

363
00:23:34,040 --> 00:23:39,340
Sayonara itsuka wa kuru ka mo shirenu

364
00:23:39,340 --> 00:23:45,560
Kisetsu wa sore demo meguri megutte'ku

365
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:53,200
Chiisaku mayotte mo aruite'ku
Kimi to aruite'ku

366
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:57,740
Sore daku wa kawaranaide iyou ne

367
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:03,160
The truth stands between
two opposing mirrors,

368
00:24:03,220 --> 00:24:06,120
each casting reflections
of outrage and joy.

369
00:24:06,560 --> 00:24:09,340
When unexpectedly
confronted by his forsaken past,

370
00:24:09,500 --> 00:24:11,820
the young man is forced to resolve issues

371
00:24:11,860 --> 00:24:14,280
that have laid hidden within
the shadows of his anger.

372
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:17,940
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

373
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:21,740
Episode 20: Father Before the Grave.

374
00:24:22,680 --> 00:24:27,980
It's not necessary to shed tears.
A person can still cry without them.
